# Mesh Hop (P2b, the shell; P3, the pages): Home is a list (Chats, Contacts, Settings, with a chevron and a short state each), the
# header has the Esc button, the caption line says the board and the notices; a page has the same header and its Esc goes back to
# Home, where it asks "Quit Mesh Hop?". Contacts and Settings (and their sub-pages) fill the width of the screen (P3); Chats is still a
# 640 px column (the stage) centred under the shell. At the five sizes, no board (the app offline). Taps go by label (a first tap
# on a row selects it, the second opens it), a tap beside the stage of Chats does nothing, the keys come through the shared keyboard
# bridge. `check` runs the shared layout checks on the pages of the full width (rows 7 mm, list rows 5 mm, buttons 9 mm, nothing
# off the screen or under the header); Chats is not checked here until P4 (mesh-hop-script `check` holds its shell to the rules).
title Mesh Hop: Home, the shell and the pages at five sizes
env MESHHOP_DATA /tmp/mesh-hop-scene-data
env MESHHOP_PORT /nonexistent/ttyMH
env MESHHOP_ONLINE 0
sizes 640x480 800x480 720x720 1024x600 1280x720

wait 900
expect text "Chats"
expect text "Contacts"
expect text "Settings"
expect text "Esc"
expect notext "Map"
expect notext "Terminal"
expect notext "More"
expect noquit

# Contacts from Home: a first tap selects the row, the second opens it. One action bar: Filter, Sort, More
tap "Contacts"
tap "Contacts"
wait 400
expect text "More"
expect notext "Zero-hop"
check contacts
# More opens the menu with the board's actions; Cancel closes it
tap "More"
wait 400
expect text "Zero-hop"
check more-menu
tap "Cancel"
wait 300
expect notext "Zero-hop"

# the Esc button of a page goes back to Home
tap "Esc"
wait 400
expect notext "More"
expect text "Settings"

# Settings, a row of its list opens the packet log (a sub-page: a first tap selects the row, the second opens it); the header Esc
# goes back to Settings, then Home
tap "Settings"
tap "Settings"
wait 400
expect text "Node name"
check settings
tap "Packet log"
tap "Packet log"
wait 300
expect text "Clear"
check packet-log
tap "Esc"
wait 400
expect notext "Clear"
expect text "Node name"

# the keys through cp0_lvgl's queue and the app's key bridge: Tab goes to the next page (Settings -> Chats -> Contacts)
key tab
wait 300
expect text "Search messages"
# beside the stage of Chats (the letterbox): nothing happens
@800x480 tapxy 0.03 0.5
@720x720 tapxy 0.5 0.95
@1024x600 tapxy 0.05 0.5
@1280x720 tapxy 0.05 0.5
expect text "Search messages"
key tab
expect text "More"
# Esc of the keyboard goes back to Home; a second short Esc at Home never quits: it says how to leave (in the caption line)
key esc
wait 300
expect notext "More"
key esc
expect text "Hold Esc 3 s to exit"
expect noquit

# the header's Esc at Home asks first: Cancel stays, Quit leaves (a touch-only board has no other way out)
tap "Esc"
wait 600
expect text "Quit Mesh Hop?"
expect noquit
tap "Cancel"
wait 400
expect notext "Quit Mesh Hop?"
expect noquit
tap "Esc"
wait 600
expect text "Quit Mesh Hop?"
tap "Quit"
wait 400
expect quit
